Once upon a time, in the shadowy depths of Stranglethorn Vale, a Gnome Warlock named Kael sought out a Succubus for his questing. He had heard tales of her cunning and adaptability, traits that made her a better companion than the often-overlooked Voidwalker. Kael, a skilled mage, was drawn to the Succubus not just for her abilities, but for the unique bond they shared—a partnership that allowed them to navigate the Vale’s dangers with ease. The Succubus, with her stealth and agility, proved invaluable in both combat and exploration. Though Voidwalkers were seen as more powerful, the Succubus’s versatility and charm made her the preferred choice. Kael’s story became a legend, proving that sometimes, the best companions are those who are underestimated. 

In the end, the Succubus’s skill in deception and adaptability made her the go-to choice, even as Voidwalkers were often seen as the stronger option. [end of text]


